## C++ Examples And Binaries

Run these commands from the directory containing this project's `CCGO.toml`:

```bash
ccgo run --example basic
ccgo run --example basic -- --help
ccgo run --example basic --release --build-only
```

The starter in `examples/basic/main.cpp` is a standalone C++ program. Examples
use `[[example]]`; executable tools use `[[bin]]` and `ccgo run --bin <name>`.
Unconfigured examples can be discovered as `examples/<name>.cpp`, `.cc`, `.cxx`,
or `examples/<name>/main.cpp`, `main.cc`, `main.cxx`.
These commands build for the local host, with outputs under `target/run/`.
The platform application in `examples/app/` uses its own Gradle/Xcode tooling.

